// Title: Hijack Legit RDP Session to Move Laterally
// Sigma ID: 52753ea4-b3a0-4365-910d-36cff487b789
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Samir Bousseaden
// Date: 2019-02-21 | Modified: 2021-11-27
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1219.002
// Description: Detects the usage of tsclient share to place a backdoor on the RDP source machine's startup
//   folder
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - Internal Research
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_tsclient_filewrite_startup.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceFileEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\mstsc.exe" and FolderPath contains "\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Start Menu\\Programs\\Startup\\"
